<section class="page-hero">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free Meta Tag Generator</h1>
    <p>This <strong>free meta tag generator</strong> builds a complete, ready-to-paste HTML head block — title, description, canonical, viewport, and social tags — in seconds. No signup, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div>
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="mt-form" onsubmit="return false;" aria-label="Meta tag generator form">
        <div>
          <label for="mt-title">Page title <span id="mt-title-count" class="llms-status"></span></label>
          <input type="text" id="mt-title" placeholder="Your Page Title — Brand Name" value="Contomatix — Link Building & SEO Services">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="mt-desc">Meta description <span id="mt-desc-count" class="llms-status"></span></label>
          <textarea id="mt-desc" placeholder="A one to two sentence summary of the page.">Contomatix helps brands grow organic traffic through link building, guest posting, on-page and off-page SEO, and keyword research.</textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="mt-url">Canonical URL</label>
          <input type="text" id="mt-url" placeholder="https://example.com/page" value="https://contomatix.com/">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="mt-author">Author (optional)</label>
          <input type="text" id="mt-author" placeholder="Company or writer name">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="mt-robots">Robots directive</label>
          <select id="mt-robots">
            <option value="index, follow">index, follow (default — allow indexing)</option>
            <option value="noindex, follow">noindex, follow (hide from search, keep link equity flowing)</option>
            <option value="noindex, nofollow">noindex, nofollow (fully hidden)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head">
        <strong>Generated &lt;head&gt; tags</strong>
        <span id="mt-status" class="llms-status">Live</span>
      </div>
      <pre id="mt-output" class="llms-output" style="max-height:320px;"></pre>
      <div class="llms-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="mt-copy">Copy</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="mt-download">Download .html</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container llms-explainer">

    <h2>Which Meta Tags Actually Matter</h2>
    <p>Not every meta tag carries equal weight. Title and description directly shape your search snippet and click-through rate. Canonical prevents duplicate-content confusion when the same content is reachable at more than one URL. Viewport is required for mobile usability, which Google treats as a baseline ranking signal. Robots directives control whether a page is indexed at all — get this one wrong and the rest doesn't matter.</p>

    <h2>Title and Description Length Guidelines</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:16px 0; font-size:0.95rem;">
        <thead>
          <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid currentColor;">
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Tag</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Recommended length</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Title</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">50–60 characters</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Meta description</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">150–160 characters</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Use our <a href="/tools/serp-snippet-preview">SERP Snippet Preview tool</a> to see exactly how a title and description will render in Google before publishing.</p>

    <h2>Common Meta Tag Mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>Duplicate titles across pages</strong> — every indexable page should have a unique title; templated titles that only vary by one word confuse both readers and search engines</li>
      <li><strong>A canonical URL pointing to the wrong page</strong> — this can accidentally tell Google to index a different page entirely instead of the one you meant</li>
      <li><strong>Missing viewport tag</strong> — without it, mobile browsers render the page as a shrunk desktop layout instead of a responsive one</li>
      <li><strong>Accidentally leaving noindex on a page after launch</strong> — a common cause of pages that mysteriously never appear in search results</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Free Meta Tag Generator FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need all of these tags on every page?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Title, description, canonical, and viewport are worth having on every indexable page. Author tags are optional and mainly useful for content with clear individual bylines.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What's the difference between canonical and robots noindex?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Canonical tells search engines which URL is the "master" version when the same content exists at multiple addresses. Noindex tells them not to show the page in search results at all, regardless of duplication.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Should every page use "index, follow"?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>For content you want found in search, yes. Use noindex for internal utility pages, thank-you pages, or duplicate/thin content you don't want competing with your main pages.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where do these tags go in my HTML?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Inside the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section of your page, before the closing <code>&lt;/head&gt;</code> tag.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool store or send my data anywhere?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Everything is generated in your browser with JavaScript — nothing is uploaded, logged, or stored on any server, including ours.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Want every page's metadata optimized?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix audits and fixes on-page SEO across your entire site.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

